BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250305T133000Z
DTEND:20250305T154500Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T071244Z
UID:36usdouv839d4jvuo5b7ebi3l3@google.com
CREATED:20250221T125437Z
DESCRIPTION:<strong>Speaker: Masaki Hori (Imperial College London)</strong>
 \n\nWe propose the first laser spectroscopy of an atom containing a kaon at
  DAPHNE\, which may eventually allow the precision on the charged kaon mass
  to be improved by 2 to 3 orders of magnitude compared to now\, and establi
 sh upper limits on beyond-the-standard model forces that may arise between 
 kaons and the other constituent particles of the atom. Metastable kaonic he
 lium is a three-body atom consisting of a helium nucleus\, an electron\, an
 d kaon occupying a Rydberg state. The atom has an anomalously long lifetime
  of 10 ns which makes it amenable to laser spectroscopy. Quantum electrodyn
 amics calculations for these atoms currently achieve parts-per-billion scal
 e precision. We have carried out similar experiments at the Antiproton Dece
 lerator of CERN for many years and determined the antiproton-to-electron ma
 ss ratio to a precision of 8 parts in 10^10\; laser spectroscopy of pionic 
 he (View Full evento Description Here: /event/determination-of-the-charged-
 kaon-mass-by-laser-spectroscopy-of-kaonic-helium-atoms-at-daphne/)
LAST-MODIFIED:20250221T125437Z
LOCATION:Aula Salvini
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Determination of the charged kaon mass by laser spectroscopy of kao
 nic helium atoms at DAPHNE
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250623T070000Z
DTEND:20250625T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260729T071244Z
UID:indico-event-46674@agenda.infn.it
URL:https://agenda.infn.it/event/46674/
CREATED:20250524T154042Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop aims to bring together experimentalists and theor
 ists at the forefront of exotic atom research\, with a special focus on kao
 nic atoms. It will serve as a dynamic forum to discuss the latest results f
 rom the SIDDHARTA-2 experiment at the DAFNE collider\, explore new theoreti
 cal insights\, and shape the future of the field. Participants will also ex
 amine upcoming opportunities at other leading international facilities such
  as J-PARC and CERN. Beyond advancing our understanding of exotic atoms\, t
 he workshop will highlight the profound impact of their study on particle a
 nd nuclear physics\, astrophysics\, and the very foundations of physics\, f
 ostering new ideas and collaborations across disciplines.\nWe dedicate this
  workshop to the memory of Prof. Carlo Guaraldo and Dr. Johann Zmeskal\, wh
 ose contributions and passion for exotic atom research continue to inspire 
 us.\n\n \nZOOM LINK for remote participation: TBA\n \nChairs:\nCatalina Cur
 ceanu\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\n \nLocal Organizers:\nMihail Iliescu\,
  INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nSimone Manti\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nD
 iana Laura Sirghi\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nFlorin Sirghi\, INFN-LNF\,
  Frascati\, Italy\nAlessandro Scordo\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nFrances
 co Sgaramella\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nMagdalena Skurzok\, Jagielloni
 an University\, Krakow\, Poland and INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\nLuca De Pa
 olis\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\n \n \nSecretariat:\nAlessandra Tamborri
 no Orsini\, INFN-LNF\, Frascati\, Italy\n \n.     \n\nhttps://agenda.infn.i
 t/event/46674/
LAST-MODIFIED:20250616T163522Z
LOCATION:Aula Salvini (Laboratori Nazionali di Frascati INFN)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Workshop on Fundamental Physics with Exotic Atoms
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
